cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Fidetype, please cite it with the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "Fidetype: open-source toolkit for brain and body-signal typing"
abstract: >-
  Fidetype is an open-source toolkit for turning brain and muscle signals
  (EEG, MEG, EMG and implant recordings) into text. Its trust layer types
  text only when it is confident, and it reports how often it is wrong.
  It works with your own decoder, and it writes the open NeuralTextStream
  (NTS) format for decoder output. Fidetype is research software, not a
  medical device.
authors:
